# No trailing slash (#168): `node_modules/` matches a directory only. A worktree set up with
# `ln -s .../princess-pi-packages/node_modules` has a SYMLINK here, which that pattern does not
# match — so `git add -A` committed it on four branches before anyone noticed. Symlinking also
# corrupts the build: bun bakes the resolved path into bundle comments, turning
# `// node_modules/wcwidth/index.js` into `// ../../../princess-pi-packages/node_modules/...`,
# dirtying the tracked bins on every build. Give each worktree a real `bun install` — it hardlinks
# from the global cache, which is the whole reason this repo standardised on bun.
node_modules
.pi/

# bun-only repo: bun.lock is authoritative. A stray `npm install` writes this
# (even with --no-save) — ignore it so it can't dirty the tree or get committed.
package-lock.json

debug/
sessions/
*.log
tmp/

# oauth2-proxy live secrets (real cfg holds client_secret/cookie_secret) — keep only .example
infra/deploy/oauth2-proxy-live-serve.cfg


# generated .mjs bins are TRACKED (committed) — required for npm install -g from GitHub
# (pacote respects .gitignore; gitignored bins would be missing from the tarball).
# NEVER EDIT THESE BY HAND — edit the .ts source, then bun run build.
# bin/patch-pi-widgets.mjs is handwritten source, not generated.
